        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0418" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg334"/>

                <head>No. 165.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Phelps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 11,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 289.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your telegram of the 9th
                    instant, in regard to the fisheries question, I transmit to you herewith a copy
                    of a note which I addressed to Sir Lionel West yesterday on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d169-a1.xml" xpointer="d169-a1"/>
            </div>
